  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "ambient: slow, sustained chords that change every four bars and swell in and out, with a sparse high bell far back in the room — no drums, no pulse",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Sixteen bars: four chords on a held ensemble, each four bars long and voiced wide, swelling in over a beat and out over two. Over it an immersed bell, one note every few bars, above 2 kHz — the top octave the research found missing from the ambient key. Plays under the Ambient key, where the drums are off; the row asks for no drums and claims no rhythm."
